WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.080
In Deuteronomy, the Torah sets
life and death before the people,

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.480
and says: choose life.

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:10.620
In Genesis, Abraham questions
God over the city of Sodom:

4
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.990
shall not the Judge of
all the earth do justly?

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.770
And in Exodus, the Hebrew midwives
refuse the king of Egypt's command.

6
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.160
So if Jews are free to choose,
can conscience overrule God's law?

7
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.990
In this mission, you'll see how
Jewish thinkers explain free will,

8
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.270
from Maimonides to Spinoza.

9
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.240
Then you'll compare how
Orthodox and Reform Jews,

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.270
and the philosopher Kant, weigh
conscience against the law.

11
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.760
Your mission: find out how far conscience
can overrule God's law in Jewish thought.
